# Diamond-inspired melee switches (docs/plan-melee-top5.md, MMOVE-22, MMOVE-23, MGUN-23, BENCH-154).
# Leigh 2026-10-31: "what can we explore in the cloud today to add to these? We have exceptionally
# strong reference bots to be inspired by, I'd like something to move us even 0.5 APS", then
# "Survival helps so this is a good line". Diamond (5th, 70.09 live) ships its source (zlib-style
# licence); three of its ideas, each our own build on master's melee (the surfer MMOVE-15 and the
# cross-learning MMOVE-19 on), each a switch off a team only:
#   aa      the baseline (master)
#   bb      its A/A copy
#   dm      mdmg, MMOVE-22: each opponent's risk term weighs by (the damage its bullets have done to
#           Hadur over the battle + 10) x its mean distance, the weights averaging 1 over the living
#           opponents; without it a hit is remembered for 100 ticks
#   la      mlat, MMOVE-23: the crowd's lateral weight 1.0 in place of 0.5 (a point straight at or
#           away from an opponent counts double, not half again)
# Cloud smoke (12 census fields x 2 seeds, seeds 3251-3252, docs/bench/local/dia-smoke.md, no A/A arm):
# dm +0.44 +- 0.58 (energy entering the endgame +3.9, skips -5%), la +0.20 +- 0.75, ea -0.11 +- 0.49 with
# skips +26% and 4 less energy entering the endgame. ea is built and kept as an arm (mavg) but not carded:
# the smoke already fails it on the card's skip bar. The card runs dm and la.
# Each build fights the 46 census fields x 6 fresh seeds alone (3253-3258, clear of the smoke's 3251-3252; 276 battles, 1,104 in
# all, about 1.8 h at ~620 battles/h) at the machine's melee width and CPU constant. The read pairs
# bb with aa (A/A, within +-0.25) and each arm with the mean of aa and bb (--base2), battle for
# battle. Melee only: the switches act off a team, so the duel and team play are untouched.
# Verdict: an arm passes with its 95% low end above 0 (--gain 0, the melee gate since 2026-10-31),
# Hadur's share of others outlived no more than 1 point lower and the 1-30 endgame wins no more than
# 3 points lower; if its skipped turns a battle rise more than 20% over aa's it fails whatever its
# APS (read from the arm reports). The card ends in a results PR on claude/pc-melee-dia-results
# whatever the verdict; the melee thread reads it.
#   ./queue.sh run pc-melee-dia        (or  .\queue.ps1 run pc-melee-dia)
# Run it from master, one bench queue at a time:
#   git checkout master && git pull
# diprep reads the version from hadur-robot/pom.xml, so a bump cannot point the card at stale
# jars, and fixes the width and version in work/, so a resumed card never mixes host profiles or
# reads another version's battles. Prep clears the arms' battle folders, since it rebuilds their jars.
# Stop rules (docs/bench/watch.md), halts only, each keeping every battle fought: fails 20 and
# stall 30m on each arm (each arm is its own single-arm step, so `dead` cannot be read). A halt
# leaves that arm's remaining battles (up to 276) and every later arm unrun (up to 828 if aa
# halts); the cause is fixed and the card resumed, and the halted arm refights all its 276
# battles (a single-arm run does not read back a stopped run's; up to ~27 min). No futility or skips rule: the paired read needs
# the baselines whole, and melee skips are read from the arm reports against aa's.

# DONE 2026-10-31 (PR #503): dm PASSED +0.43 +- 0.17 (low end +0.26; endgame wins +0.7, others outlived
# +0.5, energy at the endgame +1.8, skips +8%), la FAILED +0.00 +- 0.16, bb clean +0.08. MMOVE-22 now
# ships on, so on master the dm build is the aa robot: a fresh run of this card reads dm as an A/A
# copy, not as an arm (as xh on pc-melee-scal).
set OUT = ../docs/bench/local

diprep | git checkout -q master && V=$(sed -n 's:.*<robot.release>\(.*\)</robot.release>.*:\1:p' ../hadur-robot/pom.xml) && test -n "$V" && C=${MELEE_WORKERS} && for a in aa bb dm la; do rm -f bisect/hadur117.Hadur_"$V"$a.jar; done && bash ./build-ablation.sh aa && bash ./build-ablation.sh bb && bash ./build-ablation.sh mdmg && bash ./build-ablation.sh mlat && mkdir -p work && rm -rf work/melee-dia-"$V"-aa work/melee-dia-"$V"-bb work/melee-dia-"$V"-dm work/melee-dia-"$V"-la && echo "$V" > work/melee-dia.version && for a in aa bb dm la; do test -f bisect/hadur117.Hadur_"$V"$a.jar && sed -e "s/@V@/$V/g" -e "s/@A@/$a/g" -e "s/@C@/$C/g" plans/melee-dia.args > work/melee-dia-$a.args || exit 1; done && rm -f ${OUT}/melee-dia-*.md && for f in melee-census-317/f*.txt; do ./fetch-opponents.sh --set "$f" || exit 1; done && mvn -q compile
diaa   | mvn -q exec:java "-Dexec.args=@work/melee-dia-aa.args"
  after: diprep
  watch: battles=276
  stop: fails 20
  stop: stall 30m
dibb   | mvn -q exec:java "-Dexec.args=@work/melee-dia-bb.args"
  after: diaa
  watch: battles=276
  stop: fails 20
  stop: stall 30m
didm   | mvn -q exec:java "-Dexec.args=@work/melee-dia-dm.args"
  after: dibb
  watch: battles=276
  stop: fails 20
  stop: stall 30m
dila   | mvn -q exec:java "-Dexec.args=@work/melee-dia-la.args"
  after: didm
  watch: battles=276
  stop: fails 20
  stop: stall 30m
diread | V=$(cat work/melee-dia.version) && test -n "$V" && W=work/melee-dia-"$V" && { python3 tools/melee_s0.py screen "$W"-aa --base2 "$W"-bb --arm bb="$W"-bb --arm dm="$W"-dm --arm la="$W"-la --census melee-census-317.txt --seeds 6 --gain 0 --survival-slack 1 --out ${OUT}/melee-dia-read.md --title "Diamond-inspired melee switches on $V" || true; } && test -s ${OUT}/melee-dia-read.md
  after: dila
dipr   | bash tools/open_results_pr.sh claude/pc-melee-dia-results "Diamond-inspired melee switches (MMOVE-22, MMOVE-23, MGUN-23)" ${OUT}/melee-dia-read.md $(ls ${OUT}/melee-dia-aa.md ${OUT}/melee-dia-bb.md ${OUT}/melee-dia-dm.md ${OUT}/melee-dia-la.md 2>/dev/null)
  after: diread
